#items(((runs: ((emph: "bold", text: "Fanatic:"), (emph: "", text: " Fanatics deploy following the rules for Hidden models. However, they are not revealed like other Hidden models, but instead follow the rules below:")), sub: (((emph: "bold", text: "Release the Fanatics:"), (emph: "", text: " Fanatics are automatically released when an enemy unit comes to within 8\" of the concealing unit's Line of Sight. The moving unit stops immediately (fliers land). Once the Fanatic's movement has been resolved, the unit can continue their move (unless panicked). When a Fanatic is released, you may choose the direction in which it travels, and the point on the concealing unit from which it starts. Fanatics move 2D6\" using the rules for Random Movement, measured from the base of its unit. After release, Fanatics are treated as individual units. In your subsequent turns they must move in the Compulsory Moves subphase using the Random Movement special rule, but they always move in a random direction.")), ((emph: "bold", text: "Splat!:"), (emph: "", text: " If a Fanatic's move would bring it into contact with another unit, then he moves through rather than stopping. If the Fanatic ever ends its move over a unit, place it 1\" beyond the unit in the direction it was moving. If this is also over a unit it should be placed 1\" beyond that unit, repeating the process until it is no longer touching any models. When this happens, units between where the Fanatic ended its move do not take any damage. When a Fanatic moves through any unit it inflicts D6 Strength 5 Armour Piercing (1) hits.")), ((emph: "bold", text: "Force of Destruction:"), (emph: "", text: " Fanatics cannot be charged, but models can move into contact with them. Any unit that does so takes 2D6 Strength 5 hits with the Armour Piercing (1) special rule. The Fanatic model is then removed, and the unit may carry on with its move.")), ((emph: "bold", text: "Out of Control:"), (emph: "", text: " A Fanatic is removed immediately as a casualty when:")))), (runs: ((emph: "", text: "It contacts a piece of terrain of any kind that's not open ground."),), sub: ()), (runs: ((emph: "", text: "It contacts another Fanatic (both Fanatics are removed)."),), sub: ()), (runs: ((emph: "", text: "It moves off a table edge."),), sub: ()), (runs: ((emph: "", text: "It rolls a double for movement. This does not apply the first time the Fanatic moves."),), sub: ()), (runs: ((emph: "", text: "Any unit moves into contact with the Fanatic."),), sub: ())))
#field("UPGRADE", "")
#items(((runs: ((emph: "bold", text: "Thwackwheezer Puffshrooms:"), (emph: "", text: " Twackwheezer Puffshrooms replace the Fanatic's normal Strength 5 Hits. All models Hit must pass a Toughness test or suffer a Wound which Ignores Armour Saves. In addition, all units where the majority of the models are within 6\" of a Fanatic with this upgrade count as being in soft cover.")), sub: ()),))
#field("OPTIONS", "")
#items(((runs: ((emph: "", text: "Each individual Fanatic may replace giant ball and chain with Twackwheezer Puffshrooms free"),), sub: ()),))
#field("NOTES", "")
#items(((runs: ((emph: "", text: "Fanatics may only be taken as upgrades in units of Night Goblin Gitz, not as stand-alone units. Victory Points are rewarded for each slain Fanatic individually."),), sub: ()),))

